💡 **SUGGESTION: file is not `dart format` clean**

`dart format --set-exit-if-changed test/settings_page_test.dart` reports two spots that the formatter would rewrite (verified with Flutter 3.47.7 / Dart 3.13 formatter):

1. **Line 34** — the single-line `expect(...)` is 103 columns and gets wrapped:

```dart
// current
expect(find.descendant(of: find.byType(AppBar), matching: find.text('Settings')), findsOneWidget);

// formatted
expect(
  find.descendant(of: find.byType(AppBar), matching: find.text('Settings')),
  findsOneWidget,
);
```

2. **Lines 25–28** — the `menuTiles` helper uses the pre-3.7 cascading style; the current formatter collapses it to:

```dart
List<ListTile> menuTiles(WidgetTester tester) => tester
    .widgetList<ListTile>(find.byType(ListTile))
    .toList(growable: false);
```

Running `dart format test/settings_page_test.dart` fixes both; the other changed files are already format-clean.

💡 **SUGGESTION: consider a golden test for the settings screen**

The project has golden coverage for the other full pages (`test/collection_page_golden_test.dart`, `test/collection_item_details_page_golden_test.dart`) and `test/flutter_test_config.dart` loads the real MaterialIcons/Roboto fonts specifically "so goldens are deterministic and readable".

`SettingsPage` is fully static (no network, no images to race), so a golden would be cheap and would lock in the visual layout of the profile header above the menu:

```dart
testWidgets('settings page matches the golden', (tester) async {
  tester.view.devicePixelRatio = 1.0;
  tester.view.physicalSize = const Size(390, 844);
  addTearDown(tester.view.reset);

  await tester.pumpWidget(const MaterialApp(home: SettingsPage()));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();

  await expectLater(
    find.byType(SettingsPage),
    matchesGoldenFile('goldens/settings_page.png'),
  );
});
```

Optional polish — the existing widget tests already cover structure, order and tap behavior, so this does not block merge.

